🎯 Interview Insight — Most Important
Your solution demonstrates an important concurrency idea:
The threads don't merely need mutual exclusion; they need coordination.

synchronized gives you:
Mutual Exclusion
while:
wait()
notify()
give you:
Thread Coordination
Together:
synchronized
     +
wait()
     +
notify()
     +
shared state
     ↓
Controlled Alternating Execution
And in your specific implementation, number acts as the shared progress state while turn acts as the shared ownership state.
